### What issue are you seeing?

The official `plugin-eval` 0.1.2 event summarizer expects tool activity at the event root. Current `codex exec --json` streams wrap activity inside `item` objects under `item.started` and `item.completed`.

As a result, nested `command_execution` and `web_search` items can be omitted from tool-call and shell-command telemetry. Failed commands represented by `status: "failed"` or a nonzero `exit_code` can also be missed, even when the enclosing turn completes successfully.

This creates a misleading success signal: the benchmark process and turn can complete while activity counts remain incomplete.

### What steps can reproduce the bug?

Pass a current-style event sequence to `summarizeCodexEvents`:

```jsonl
{"type":"thread.started","thread_id":"thread-current"}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"command-1","type":"command_execution","command":"npm test","status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"command-1","type":"command_execution","command":"npm test","status":"completed","exit_code":0}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"search-1","type":"web_search","query":"official documentation"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"search-1","type":"web_search","query":"official documentation"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"command-2","type":"command_execution","command":"npm run missing","status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"command-2","type":"command_execution","command":"npm run missing","status":"failed","exit_code":1}}
{"type":"turn.completed","usage":{"input_tokens":10,"output_tokens":5,"total_tokens":15}}
```

The unpatched parser inspects the outer `item.started` and `item.completed` event types instead of the nested activity objects, so it does not reliably record the command executions or web search.

### What is the expected behavior?

The summarizer should:

- inspect the nested `item` object;
- count completed activity only, avoiding double-counting the matching `item.started` event;
- report 3 tool calls;
- report 2 shell commands;
- report 1 failed shell command;
- recognize `command_execution` and `web_search` as tool types;
- preserve the completed turn and usage information.

### Additional information

Environment:

- Codex CLI 0.155.1
- Windows
- `plugin-eval` 0.1.2

A tested patch is available at:

https://github.com/okargbo11/plugins/tree/fix/plugin-eval-codex-item-telemetry

Comparison against upstream:

https://github.com/openai/plugins/compare/main...okargbo11:fix/plugin-eval-codex-item-telemetry?expand=1

Validation:

- `npm test`: 28 passed, 0 failed, 1 intentional Windows-only POSIX-fixture skip.
- Node syntax checks and `git diff --check`: passed.
- A post-patch replay of a retained 16-scenario JSONL corpus reported 107 tool calls, 103 shell commands, 29 failed shell commands, and 16 completed turns.

The same commit contains Windows path fixes related to #44090. This issue is limited to the distinct telemetry-envelope defect.
